# Regenerable line-numbered INPUT windows (~450 MB total). git-lfs is unavailable on this host,
# so these bulky per-batch window files are not tracked. They rebuild deterministically from the
# tracked manifests (*_manifest.jsonl map unit_id -> doc_id + line offsets) plus the samplers
# (build_span_units.py / build_span_units_ext.py). The annotations + span_dataset.jsonl + manifests
# below ARE tracked, so the dataset is fully usable and reproducible without these.
SPAN/
SPAN_recover/
A_boundary/
B_betagate/
B_scale/
G_sections/
W_windows/

# transient loop/run cursors
SPAN_loop_state.json
SPAN_recover_paths.json

# frozen line-embedding cache (large, regenerable)
SPAN_emb/
SPAN_linemat.npz
SPAN_pline*.npz
SPAN_pred_dl.json

# FP-validation audit samples (regenerable)
FPVAL/
FPVAL_batchpaths.json

# STRUCT structural-annotation runs (gpt-5.5 ToC+bib). Large intermediates: the historically named
# 538MB ``*_gold.jsonl`` is LLM-silver, not human gold, plus per-batch windows and the feature cache.
# The LLM annotation outputs (ann_*.json) were the expensive artifact and required an out-of-band backup
# (no git-lfs here). Code + small fitted model JSONs are tracked; the missing raw run is not reconstructable
# from Git alone.
STRUCT_2K/
STRUCT_2K_gold.jsonl
STRUCT_linemat.npz
STRUCT_batchpaths.json
STRUCT/
STRUCT2/
STRUCT2_FT/
BAKEOFF_gpt55/
SMOKE_gpt55/
